  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nHTML's `<source>` elements are able to query viewport width with the [`media`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/source#media) attribute to swap image sources based on device size. Now that [container queries are part of Baseline 2023](https://caniuse.com/css-container-queries), `<source>` attributes should be able to swap image sources based on the size of a parent container as well\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nDIY JavaScript solutions can alter the `src` attribute of `<img>` elements, but this still requires the rapid-fire callbacks of a `resizeObserver` to handle. JS-based solutions could be improved with a `window.matchMedia` analog for container queries as proposed [here](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/6205), but a native HTML solution would be ideal.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nSimilar to the existing `media` attribute, a new `container` attribute would be added and its value used to query the inline size of a container. This would query the width of the containing `picture` element to select the preferred source.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<picture>\r\n  <source srcset=\"image-wide.png\" container=\"(width > 800px)\" />\r\n  <source srcset=\"image-medium.png\" container=\"(width > 600px)\" />\r\n  <img src=\"image-narrow.png\" alt=\"alt text\" />\r\n</picture>\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlternatively, the container could also accept a `<container-name>` value that's been defined in CSS to instead query some container higher in the DOM.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<picture>\r\n  <source srcset=\"image-wide.png\" container=\"component (width > 800px)\" />\r\n  <source srcset=\"image-medium.png\" container=\"component (width > 600px)\" />\r\n  <img src=\"image-narrow.png\" alt=\"alt text\" />\r\n</picture>\r\n```\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
